import tests/games/studio/application.dl
import tests/games/three_dimensional.dl

to position the camera from {spatial camera:view} in {graphics frame:frame}:
    reset the camera in frame
    rotate the camera in frame by -view's yaw degrees around x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
    move the camera in frame by x -view's position's x, y -view's position's y and z -view's position's z

to draw a cube at {spatial position:position} with size {floating-point number:size} in {graphics frame:frame}:
    set half to size / 2.0
    save the model transform in frame
    move the model in frame by x position's x, y position's y and z position's z
    start triangles in frame

    use vertex color red 220, green 80 and blue 80 in frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z half to frame

    use vertex color red 80, green 220 and blue 80 in frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z -half to frame

    use vertex color red 80, green 80 and blue 220 in frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z -half to frame

    use vertex color red 220, green 220 and blue 80 in frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z half to frame

    use vertex color red 220, green 80 and blue 220 in frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y half and z -half to frame

    use vertex color red 80, green 220 and blue 220 in frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z -half to frame
    add a vertex at x half, y -half and z half to frame
    add a vertex at x -half, y -half and z half to frame

    finish triangles in frame
    restore the model transform in frame

to paint the cube on {a pointer to UI canvas frame:canvas}:
    set session to the spatial study in (canvas's instance)
    set frame to canvas's frame
    use a perspective of 77.3 degrees from 0.1 to 200.0 on canvas
    position the camera from (session's camera) in frame
    rotate the model in frame by 25.0 degrees around x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
    rotate the model in frame by (35.0 + session's elapsed * 18.0) degrees around x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
    draw a cube at (a position with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) with size 3.0 in frame

set session to a new spatial study from (a camera at (a position with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 8.0) facing 0.0 degrees with speed 0.2 and turn rate 2.0)
set session's painter to (the function named "paint the cube on $") as a pointer
explore (the address of session) named "Color cube" in spatial studio
